  "name": "Socopé (São Tomé dance rhythm)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Dance rhythm of São Tomé that arose, like puíta and danço-congo, among the islands' slave-descended population; in the 1970s Os Úntués and other conjuntos set it for electric guitars and dance band, mixing in European pop and soukous elements. This entry models that recorded conjunto form as a live-room tape capture.",
